.Martin. wrote:
> 
> 1. What am I supposed to do with a surplus of weapon/armour? Shall I
> just drop some daggers that I don't use?

Drop the weapons that you cannot use efficiently. As a valkyrie that you
are playing you can focus on a single long sword and a bunch of daggers,
anything from 15-20 daggers is nice to have. Enhance your skill in those
weapons as soon as you are allowed to. Armour is heavy, so pick the best
pieces, the ones that reduce your AC value most, though be careful with
cursed items as mentioned upthread; check its BUC status before you try
to put it on.

> 2. How do you search for hidden doors ('s')? I've read that constantly
> tapping on the 's' key is discouraged from. Someone recommended
> eg. 'n10s' which will search 10x. Now my question is wether it'll search
> ten times in the square I'm standing now or will it search as I move on
> to some other places. In other words, is that command placed in one unit
> of time /one turn or it uses up 10 turns / units of time? I hope you'll
> understand what I mean.

The command n10s will search the square that you're standing on and its
eigth adjacent squares at most 10 times. As soon as you find something
the search is interrupted, so you may end with only 2 or 3 turns spent,
despite having used the counted search command. (It's also interrupted
on some other events, as mentioned.) You should always make use of the
counted search as long as you use small numbers like 10 or 20, because
there are, for example, dead ends in corridors where you think must be
a secret passage but ther isn't, and if you type n200s those 200 turns
will be spent, and if no monsters appear to interrupt your search, you
may get hungrier and get in troubles subsequently. (BTW, the command ^A
(Ctrl-A) repeats the last command, so n10s and then ^A will search 20
times, for example.)

